WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.350
Service path. Your own environment.

2
00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:10.466
How do I get an environment I can use?

3
00:00:12.024 --> 00:00:13.794
Start with spi check.

4
00:00:14.024 --> 00:00:19.624
It confirms the tools spi drives, and that
your Azure sign-in may create resource

5
00:00:19.624 --> 00:00:22.674
groups, clusters and role assignments.

6
00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:26.674
Then spi up, with a name
for your environment.

7
00:00:26.824 --> 00:00:30.424
It builds your stack as one resource
group in your subscription.

8
00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:34.984
Thirty-seven minutes later,
in this take, it returned,

9
00:00:34.984 --> 00:00:37.714
with Flux reconciling in the background.

10
00:00:39.702 --> 00:00:43.262
spi up returns before the
environment is usable.

11
00:00:43.652 --> 00:00:45.982
Its own last lines say so:

12
00:00:46.052 --> 00:00:48.302
deployable after convergence.

13
00:00:48.532 --> 00:00:50.462
So wait for Deployable.

14
00:00:51.412 --> 00:00:56.932
spi status, with --watch,
refreshes every thirty seconds,

15
00:00:56.932 --> 00:01:01.822
and its summary reads Not deployable
while Flux is still working.

16
00:01:02.212 --> 00:01:07.022
Here it turned to Deployable twenty-two
minutes after spi up returned.

17
00:01:07.092 --> 00:01:08.942
That's the word to wait for.

18
00:01:11.432 --> 00:01:14.912
Then use it. spi info
names your endpoints:

19
00:01:14.912 --> 00:01:20.832
the gateway, where the OSDU APIs
answer, with Kibana and Airflow

20
00:01:20.832 --> 00:01:26.042
beside it. When you're done, give
the environment back with spi down.

21
00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:30.842
It keeps your managed identities,
so the next spi up reuses them.

22
00:01:33.252 --> 00:01:34.572
An easy mistake:

23
00:01:34.572 --> 00:01:36.902
the command finished, so it is ready.

24
00:01:37.212 --> 00:01:41.852
A finished spi up means the build
went through without a fatal error,

25
00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:44.102
not that an API is ready.

26
00:01:44.412 --> 00:01:49.302
Moments after it returned, the
summary still said Not deployable:

27
00:01:49.612 --> 00:01:53.622
Flux was reconciling, and
setup jobs had yet to run.

28
00:01:53.772 --> 00:01:56.822
Check with spi status --watch.

29
00:01:59.288 --> 00:02:00.488
So now you can say:

30
00:02:00.488 --> 00:02:04.168
spi up returns before the
environment is usable,

31
00:02:04.168 --> 00:02:07.778
and spi status says when it's Deployable.

32
00:02:10.344 --> 00:02:12.954
Next: who does the stack think you are?

